  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "audio_sample_entry_box_read",
    "file": "gpac/src/isomedia/box_code_base.c",
    "description": "`audio_sample_entry_box_read` frees `ptr->esd` via `gf_isom_box_del_parent(&ptr->child_boxes, (GF_Box*)ptr->esd)` when it finds a replacement `esds` in the fallback scan path, but it does not clear all aliases to that object before later destruction. The old ESDS can remain referenced through box hierarchy state and is then reached again during recursive cleanup (`gf_isom_box_del` -> `gf_isom_box_array_del`), causing a second delete/use-after-free in `gf_isom_box_del` when reading `a->child_boxes` from already-freed memory.",
    "conditions": "Trigger requires an `mp4a`/audio sample entry where normal child parsing fails (`gf_isom_box_array_read` returns error), causing the fallback byte-scan for `esds` (lines ~4044+). If an existing `ptr->esd` is already present in `child_boxes`, the code deletes it and reparses/re-adds ESDS, but malformed structure leaves stale ownership/reference in the parent/child graph. On movie teardown (`gf_isom_delete_movie`), recursive box deletion revisits the freed ESDS pointer, producing heap-use-after-free."
  },
